    "body": "Quick pass (coordinator, read only, no build) on head `42a68699e`: the PR is a sub-PR of `side/path-kernel` and merges cleanly with it (`a875b62ea`). The body starts with `Side branch: side/path-kernel` and ends with `Refs #3752`; it has the scope, the old-against-new tables, the pins, the open items and the gates. The writer record on #3752 is released. Private files (#1749): the diff, the file list and the body have no reference to `fig8.camproj` or `testpart.sc`; the fig8 cases read the tracked `testdata/models/fig8.step` with parameters that the test states. The PR is flagged ready. It waits for the independent review.\n\nNotes for the reviewer. The safety floor applies, and the issue is `P1`: this is the first PR in which output of the kernel can reach the post (only with `CAMCRAFT_PLANNER=new`; the default is the old planner, and the pin `kernel_route_default_engine_keeps_the_old_pocket` holds that move for move).\n- Check the switch: under `new` only the 2D Pocket passes `check_engine`; Zigzag, Adaptive, rest machining, \"do not touch\" and the corner relief are refused by name; there is no silent fallback to the old planner.\n- The body does not claim that the kernel pocket is ready to be the default. Its tables show: on `fig8.step` the Inside start is refused by name (#4324); the verifier reports 6 `Crossing` findings on fig8 (#4300) and they block the post; the over-limit and full-width reads are higher than with the old planner (#4260, #4272); the lifts are fewer and each one is named. Check that each of these is in the pins as measured, and that no pin was made weaker to pass.\n- The PR changes the converter (`LevelPlan::top_z`, `APPROACH_IN_MATERIAL`, `BAD_LEVEL_TOP`) and the region adapter (`without_slivers`). Check that the sliver rule drops only a loop with no area.\n- A sync of `main` into the side branch is in work (PR to follow). The PR that merges second takes a merge of the side branch.",
